    "observationBoundary": {
      "const": "Five cases replay the debug Map Test 0 prompt from one shared in-memory core state. A deterministic session-only copy of the verified ROM replaces the existing RunMapSetupInitFunction indirect call with a 16-byte FF-padding trampoline. The trampoline sets A6 to a RAM-owned word stream and JSRs one unmodified lifecycle handler; the original disk ROM is re-hashed unchanged before the launch. Lua writes only the input word stream, CURRENT_MAP, VIEW_TARGET_ENTITY, FADING_SETTING for the bounded fade release, and two 16-bit nonasset markers at the source-derived ResetCurrentMap layout-clear boundaries. It observes handler entry/return boundaries, chronological direct H1 JSR call-site callbacks, post-handler VIEW_PLANE_A_PIXEL_X/Y, and marker comparisons; it does not observe service effects. The original handlers and unmodified direct service bodies execute in one BizHawk launch."
    },
